      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint, e.g. 'Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C10\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The capacitor will not fit the intended footprint, and if assembled, may not make proper contact or may be placed incorrectly.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C10"],
      "pins": ["C10.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C10-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "C10 pin 1 is on net 'unconnected-(C10-Pad1)' with no other connections; pin 2 is on GND.",
      "expected": "Both pins of a decoupling capacitor should be connected to the intended nets (e.g., a power rail and GND).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C10-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C10\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C10\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "C10 is electrically open and provides no decoupling or filtering; it is a non-functional component.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain anomalies: two Ethernet PHY transmit pins on U9 are shorted to ground, and C10 is a capacitor with an inductor footprint and an unconnected pin."
}

